      "id": "emergent_eu_ai_crisis_cabinet",
      "description": "In response to the repeated cyber incidents and collapsing political capital, a coalition of smaller member states pushes through the formation of an emergency EU AI Crisis Cabinet, bypassing national vetoes under Article 222. The body is granted temporary authority to coordinate cross-border AI operations, override national procurement decisions, and allocate sovereign compute resources, marking a significant but contested centralization of power.",
